    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d766">

                <pb facs="0927" n="833" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg833"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williams to Mr.
                            Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2847.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report to the
                    Department, on information received from Mr. Viondi, the advocate, that the
                    military court having under its investigation the charges against Mr. Julio
                    Sanguily and some twenty others for participation in the kidnaping of Mr.
                    Antonio Fernandez de Castro by the bandit Manuel Garcia on his plantation near
                    the towns of Bainoa and Aguacate in the year 1894, has quashed all these cases.
                    They are still pending, however, before the civil court.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramon O. Williams</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
